.SS "\fBenum\fP \fBaiImporterFlags\fP"
Mixed set of flags for \fBaiImporterDesc\fP, indicating some features common to many importers 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fIaiImporterFlags_SupportTextFlavour \fP\fP
Indicates that there is a textual encoding of the file format; and that it is supported\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIaiImporterFlags_SupportBinaryFlavour \fP\fP
Indicates that there is a binary encoding of the file format; and that it is supported\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIaiImporterFlags_SupportCompressedFlavour \fP\fP
Indicates that there is a compressed encoding of the file format; and that it is supported\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIaiImporterFlags_LimitedSupport \fP\fP
Indicates that the importer reads only a very particular subset of the file format\&. This happens commonly for declarative or procedural formats which cannot easily be mapped to \fBaiScene\fP 
.TP
\fB\fIaiImporterFlags_Experimental \fP\fP
Indicates that the importer is highly experimental and should be used with care\&. This only happens for trunk (i\&.e\&. SVN) versions, experimental code is not included in releases\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBASSIMP_API\fP const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiImporterDesc\fP * aiGetImporterDesc (const char * extension)"

.PP
